WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:04.548
You'll run the four rings,

3
00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:08.987
with exit criteria and backout
triggers set before each one starts.

4
00:00:08.987 --> 00:00:13.090
You'll keep the V P N, DirectAccess
and another security service edge

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:17.338
working beside the service during
the move, and explain branch parity.

6
00:00:17.338 --> 00:00:21.176
You'll say who is responsible and
accountable for each activity,

7
00:00:21.176 --> 00:00:22.624
and who decides closure.

8
00:00:22.624 --> 00:00:26.400
You'll assemble the five kinds of
evidence for each network finding.

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.762
And you'll compute the guide's coverage
metrics, and roll back in the guide's order.

10
00:00:30.762 --> 00:00:33.279
You need Modules 1 to 5 and their labs,

11
00:00:33.279 --> 00:00:37.725
and Zero Trust and Assessment,
chapter ten, for the closure chain.

12
00:00:37.725 --> 00:00:40.940
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production.
